1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,892
3,000 pounds of meth.

2
00:00:02,892 --> 00:00:04,243
One semi truck.

3
00:00:04,693 --> 00:00:05,983
October 9, 2020.

4
00:00:05,983 --> 00:00:09,370
A tractor-trailer pulls into the Otay Mesa

5
00:00:09,370 --> 00:00:12,031
commercial crossing in San Diego.

6
00:00:12,031 --> 00:00:15,338
On paper, it's carrying medical supplies.

7
00:00:15,788 --> 00:00:19,433
Customs officers open it up and count 1,816

8
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:22,316
packages, mixed in with the boxes.

9
00:00:22,316 --> 00:00:25,961
About 3,014 pounds of methamphetamine, plus

10
00:00:25,961 --> 00:00:27,656
heroin and fentanyl.

11
00:00:27,656 --> 00:00:31,980
More than $7 million, by the government's estimate.

12
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:35,177
Every day, long lines of trucks roll north

13
00:00:35,177 --> 00:00:36,355
across the border.

14
00:00:36,355 --> 00:00:39,691
Most of them are exactly what their paperwork says.

15
00:00:39,691 --> 00:00:42,504
So how do officers find the one that isn't?

16
00:00:42,504 --> 00:00:44,270
And how often do they miss?

17
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:47,526
This is the case file on drugs hidden in semi

18
00:00:47,526 --> 00:00:47,963
trucks.

19
00:00:50,563 --> 00:00:51,779
Start at the gate.

20
00:00:52,229 --> 00:00:55,621
Otay Mesa is San Diego's commercial port of entry.

21
00:00:55,621 --> 00:00:58,538
Cargo trucks from Tijuana line up here, and

22
00:00:58,538 --> 00:01:01,456
each one stops at a booth, where an officer

23
00:01:01,456 --> 00:01:03,898
checks the driver and the paperwork.

24
00:01:04,348 --> 00:01:07,714
On that Friday in October, at about 9:45 in

25
00:01:07,714 --> 00:01:10,924
the morning, a driver arrived with a load

26
00:01:10,924 --> 00:01:13,351
manifested as medical supplies.

27
00:01:13,801 --> 00:01:16,928
Officers sent the truck to secondary inspection.

28
00:01:16,928 --> 00:01:19,404
There, according to Customs and Border

29
00:01:19,404 --> 00:01:22,401
Protection, an imaging system showed something

30
00:01:22,401 --> 00:01:25,333
wrong in the trailer, and a drug-sniffing dog

31
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:25,854
alerted.

32
00:01:26,304 --> 00:01:29,354
Inside, among spray bottles and pipette tools,

33
00:01:29,354 --> 00:01:31,211
officers found the packages.

34
00:01:31,661 --> 00:01:32,583
The count:

35
00:01:32,583 --> 00:01:36,274
about 3,014 pounds of meth, 64 pounds of

36
00:01:36,274 --> 00:01:40,058
heroin, 29 pounds of fentanyl powder, and

37
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:43,287
almost 37 pounds of fentanyl pills.

38
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:46,052
CBP called it the second-largest

39
00:01:46,052 --> 00:01:49,234
methamphetamine bust on the southwest border

40
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:50,969
in the agency's history.

41
00:01:51,419 --> 00:01:54,939
The driver, a 47-year-old Mexican citizen, was

42
00:01:54,939 --> 00:01:58,305
arrested, and turned over to a joint team of

43
00:01:58,305 --> 00:02:01,672
Homeland Security Investigations and the DEA

44
00:02:01,672 --> 00:02:02,896
to face charges.

45
00:02:02,896 --> 00:02:05,956
Charges are allegations; he was presumed

46
00:02:05,956 --> 00:02:08,251
innocent unless proven guilty.

47
00:02:08,701 --> 00:02:11,682
The DEA's special agent in charge in San

48
00:02:11,682 --> 00:02:14,812
Diego, John Callery, said the seizure kept

49
00:02:14,812 --> 00:02:17,867
more than $7 million of deadly drugs from

50
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:19,432
entering the country.

51
00:02:20,232 --> 00:02:21,619
Then it happened again.

52
00:02:22,069 --> 00:02:23,215
May 15, 2021.

53
00:02:23,215 --> 00:02:25,420
Same commercial facility.

54
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:28,331
Same time of morning, about 9:45.

55
00:02:28,331 --> 00:02:32,388
Another tractor-trailer, manifested, again, as

56
00:02:32,388 --> 00:02:33,887
medical supplies.

57
00:02:34,337 --> 00:02:36,820
This time, a roving team of officers picked

58
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:39,649
the truck out while it was still waiting in line.

59
00:02:40,099 --> 00:02:42,115
The X-ray showed anomalies.

60
00:02:42,115 --> 00:02:44,206
A dog alerted to one pallet.

61
00:02:44,206 --> 00:02:47,491
Officers unloaded the shipment and found 120

62
00:02:47,491 --> 00:02:50,851
packages, mixed in with the legitimate goods.

63
00:02:51,301 --> 00:02:54,673
About 2,425 pounds of meth.

64
00:02:54,673 --> 00:02:57,296
Roughly $5.5 million.

65
00:02:57,746 --> 00:03:00,877
The acting director of field operations in San

66
00:03:00,877 --> 00:03:03,463
Diego, Anne Maricich, put it this way.

67
00:03:03,913 --> 00:03:07,003
Most of what officers see every day, she said,

68
00:03:07,003 --> 00:03:08,347
is legitimate cargo.

69
00:03:08,347 --> 00:03:11,369
But transnational criminal organizations will

70
00:03:11,369 --> 00:03:13,855
attempt any avenue they can think of.

71
00:03:14,655 --> 00:03:17,920
A 29-year-old Mexican man was arrested and

72
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:21,264
handed to Homeland Security Investigations.

73
00:03:21,264 --> 00:03:23,130
Charges are allegations.

74
00:03:23,130 --> 00:03:26,473
Every defendant is presumed innocent unless

75
00:03:26,473 --> 00:03:27,561
proven guilty.

76
00:03:28,011 --> 00:03:31,027
Further east, in Arizona, a record had already

77
00:03:31,027 --> 00:03:31,617
been set.

78
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:34,874
Otay Mesa. Calexico. Nogales. Pharr.

79
00:03:34,874 --> 00:03:38,305
Four commercial crossings, and five cases in

80
00:03:38,305 --> 00:03:39,085
this file.

81
00:03:39,535 --> 00:03:40,771
Nogales, Arizona.

82
00:03:40,771 --> 00:03:43,026
At the Mariposa cargo crossing,

83
00:03:43,026 --> 00:03:46,080
tractor-trailers line up to clear customs,

84
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:49,352
many of them hauling fresh produce north from

85
00:03:49,352 --> 00:03:49,861
Mexico.

86
00:03:50,311 --> 00:03:53,440
On a Saturday at the end of January, 2019, a

87
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:56,640
truck driver brought in a trailer loaded with

88
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:57,351
cucumbers.

89
00:03:57,801 --> 00:04:01,634
254 pounds of fentanyl were riding in that trailer.

90
00:04:01,634 --> 00:04:04,941
At secondary inspection, an officer scanning

91
00:04:04,941 --> 00:04:08,173
it saw anomalies in the floor, and a canine

92
00:04:08,173 --> 00:04:09,150
team alerted.

93
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:13,982
Under the cucumbers was a hidden floor compartment.

94
00:04:13,982 --> 00:04:15,787
Inside: 416 packages.

95
00:04:16,237 --> 00:04:20,105
94 of them held the fentanyl, mostly powder,

96
00:04:20,105 --> 00:04:21,512
with some pills.

97
00:04:21,512 --> 00:04:25,645
The rest was methamphetamine, about 395 pounds.

98
00:04:26,095 --> 00:04:27,611
Why does that matter?

99
00:04:27,611 --> 00:04:30,933
According to Homeland Security Investigations'

100
00:04:30,933 --> 00:04:34,039
special agent in charge, Juan Mariscal, one

101
00:04:34,039 --> 00:04:36,928
kilogram of fentanyl can produce about a

102
00:04:36,928 --> 00:04:38,372
million fatal doses.

103
00:04:38,372 --> 00:04:40,828
This load was about 114 kilograms.

104
00:04:40,828 --> 00:04:44,078
The Nogales port director, Michael Humphries,

105
00:04:44,078 --> 00:04:47,111
said an amount the size of a few grains of

106
00:04:47,111 --> 00:04:48,772
salt can kill a person.

107
00:04:49,222 --> 00:04:52,619
At the time, it was the largest fentanyl

108
00:04:52,619 --> 00:04:54,573
seizure in CBP history.

109
00:04:54,573 --> 00:04:58,310
NBC News reported it was more than twice the

110
00:04:58,310 --> 00:04:59,669
previous record:

111
00:04:59,669 --> 00:05:02,897
118 pounds, found in Nebraska in 2017.

112
00:05:03,347 --> 00:05:04,249
For scale:

113
00:05:04,249 --> 00:05:08,311
Arizona's ports of entry had seized 20 pounds

114
00:05:08,311 --> 00:05:12,103
of fentanyl in all of fiscal 2016, and 155

115
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:14,089
pounds in fiscal 2018.

116
00:05:14,089 --> 00:05:16,616
One trailer beat both years.

117
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:20,321
In 2017, according to the CDC, more than

118
00:05:20,321 --> 00:05:23,820
28,000 deaths in the United States involved

119
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:27,156
synthetic opioids other than methadone, a

120
00:05:27,156 --> 00:05:29,759
category that includes fentanyl.

121
00:05:30,209 --> 00:05:31,407
The driver was 26.

122
00:05:31,407 --> 00:05:34,336
According to the criminal complaint, he told

123
00:05:34,336 --> 00:05:37,331
officers he didn't know the drugs were there.

124
00:05:37,331 --> 00:05:39,993
He said he had picked up the load in the

125
00:05:39,993 --> 00:05:42,589
morning, checked the trailer, and found

126
00:05:42,589 --> 00:05:43,654
nothing unusual.

127
00:05:43,654 --> 00:05:46,582
He was being paid, the complaint says, about

128
00:05:46,582 --> 00:05:47,980
$36 for the delivery.

129
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:50,051
He didn't own the trailer.

130
00:05:50,051 --> 00:05:52,793
He told officers he suspected a well-dressed

131
00:05:52,793 --> 00:05:55,536
stranger who had loaded it, or the owners of

132
00:05:55,536 --> 00:05:56,409
the cucumbers.

133
00:05:56,859 --> 00:05:59,837
He was charged with possession with intent to

134
00:05:59,837 --> 00:06:00,565
distribute.

135
00:06:00,565 --> 00:06:03,081
A charge is only an accusation; he was

136
00:06:03,081 --> 00:06:05,662
presumed innocent unless proven guilty.

137
00:06:05,662 --> 00:06:08,707
Mariscal said the size of the shipment and how

138
00:06:08,707 --> 00:06:11,685
it was concealed pointed to something bigger.

139
00:06:12,135 --> 00:06:15,413
A well-organized smuggling operation, he suggested.

140
00:06:15,413 --> 00:06:17,085
Bigger than any one truck.

141
00:06:17,885 --> 00:06:20,422
Humphries made another point that day.

142
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:23,360
Most hard narcotics CBP seizes, he said, are

143
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,296
caught at the ports of entry.

144
00:06:25,296 --> 00:06:28,368
In his opinion, smugglers prefer vehicles with

145
00:06:28,368 --> 00:06:31,172
hidden compartments they can track, rather

146
00:06:31,172 --> 00:06:33,309
than crossing between the ports.

147
00:06:33,759 --> 00:06:35,615
How do they pick the one truck?

148
00:06:36,065 --> 00:06:39,465
Three tools come up in every one of these cases.

149
00:06:39,465 --> 00:06:42,298
An officer who decides a load is worth a

150
00:06:42,298 --> 00:06:43,148
second look.

151
00:06:43,148 --> 00:06:46,194
An X-ray or gamma-ray image of the trailer.

152
00:06:46,194 --> 00:06:46,902
And a dog.

153
00:06:47,352 --> 00:06:50,727
At Nogales, CBP uses a multi-energy portal, a

154
00:06:50,727 --> 00:06:52,376
drive-through scanner.

155
00:06:52,376 --> 00:06:55,751
Trucks roll through it, and the image goes to

156
00:06:55,751 --> 00:06:57,251
an officer's screen.

157
00:06:57,701 --> 00:07:00,512
What the officer is looking for is an anomaly.

158
00:07:00,512 --> 00:07:03,262
Something in the image that doesn't match the

159
00:07:03,262 --> 00:07:05,829
paperwork, like the floors in these cases.

160
00:07:06,279 --> 00:07:07,335
Then the dogs.

161
00:07:07,335 --> 00:07:10,655
CBP canine teams work the lines of vehicles.

162
00:07:10,655 --> 00:07:13,597
The dogs are trained to find narcotics,

163
00:07:13,597 --> 00:07:15,559
people, money and weapons.

164
00:07:16,009 --> 00:07:18,874
At El Paso, smaller low-energy portals scan

165
00:07:18,874 --> 00:07:21,807
passenger cars while they drive through, and

166
00:07:21,807 --> 00:07:24,606
the images go straight to officers inside.

167
00:07:25,056 --> 00:07:27,607
But here is the number that matters.

168
00:07:27,607 --> 00:07:30,372
According to the Congressional Research

169
00:07:30,372 --> 00:07:33,277
Service, as of fiscal 2024, CBP was using

170
00:07:33,277 --> 00:07:36,538
these scanners on about 15 percent of arriving

171
00:07:36,538 --> 00:07:37,813
commercial trucks.

172
00:07:38,263 --> 00:07:39,968
15 percent of trucks.

173
00:07:39,968 --> 00:07:41,916
98 percent of rail cars.

174
00:07:41,916 --> 00:07:44,514
1 percent of passenger vehicles.

175
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:47,066
Congress has asked for more.

176
00:07:47,066 --> 00:07:50,520
A law passed for fiscal 2021 required Homeland

177
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:53,748
Security to draw up a plan, with costs, for

178
00:07:53,748 --> 00:07:56,751
inspecting 100 percent of commercial and

179
00:07:56,751 --> 00:07:58,703
passenger vehicle traffic.

180
00:07:59,153 --> 00:08:02,272
Congress has been paying for more.

181
00:08:02,272 --> 00:08:06,218
In fiscal 2019 it gave CBP $570 million for

182
00:08:06,218 --> 00:08:07,961
scanning equipment.

183
00:08:07,961 --> 00:08:11,631
But by December 2024, of 150 large fixed

184
00:08:11,631 --> 00:08:15,577
systems, 50 had been installed, and 43 were

185
00:08:15,577 --> 00:08:17,137
still in storage.

186
00:08:17,587 --> 00:08:20,572
So most of the time, the first line of defense

187
00:08:20,572 --> 00:08:23,752
is still an officer's judgment, and a dog's nose.

188
00:08:24,202 --> 00:08:25,247
Then Texas.

189
00:08:25,697 --> 00:08:26,931
April 11, 2025.

190
00:08:26,931 --> 00:08:30,633
The cargo facility at the Pharr International

191
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:33,676
Bridge, in South Texas, near McAllen.

192
00:08:34,126 --> 00:08:37,164
1,600 pounds of meth, in a load of peppers.

193
00:08:37,164 --> 00:08:40,202
A tractor-trailer comes in from Mexico, and

194
00:08:40,202 --> 00:08:43,875
the paperwork says fresh bell peppers and cucumbers.

195
00:08:44,325 --> 00:08:47,165
Officers refer it for inspection, run it

196
00:08:47,165 --> 00:08:50,574
through the scanner, and bring in a canine team.

197
00:08:50,574 --> 00:08:53,627
Concealed inside the trailer: 300 packages.

198
00:08:54,077 --> 00:08:56,071
The final weight:

199
00:08:56,071 --> 00:08:59,826
1,635 pounds of methamphetamine.

200
00:08:59,826 --> 00:09:04,167
CBP valued it at about $14.6 million.

201
00:09:04,617 --> 00:09:07,512
The port director, Carlos Rodriguez, said

202
00:09:07,512 --> 00:09:10,759
officers were using all tools and resources to

203
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:13,866
keep these narcotics from reaching America's

204
00:09:13,866 --> 00:09:14,430
streets.

205
00:09:14,430 --> 00:09:17,325
Homeland Security Investigations opened a

206
00:09:17,325 --> 00:09:18,313
criminal case.

207
00:09:18,763 --> 00:09:20,897
And this summer, California again.

208
00:09:21,347 --> 00:09:22,216
July 2026.

209
00:09:22,216 --> 00:09:26,475
The Calexico port of entry, across from Mexicali.

210
00:09:26,475 --> 00:09:30,126
A commercial truck pulls a flatbed trailer

211
00:09:30,126 --> 00:09:32,995
loaded with 269 bundles of rebar.

212
00:09:33,445 --> 00:09:35,963
The X-ray showed anomalies in the wooden

213
00:09:35,963 --> 00:09:37,662
floorboards of the trailer.

214
00:09:37,662 --> 00:09:38,543
A dog alerted.

215
00:09:38,993 --> 00:09:40,015
366 packages.

216
00:09:40,015 --> 00:09:43,315
Officers unloaded the rebar, unscrewed the

217
00:09:43,315 --> 00:09:46,929
